### Dispatch 13 Summary: Component Contribution via Extensions

The implementation of component contribution via Extensions has been completed, tested, and committed on branch `dispatch/13` in `/home/ubuntu/code/mesh-web-dispatch-13`.

The comprehensive report is committed at [`agent-runs/reports/13-component-contribution.md`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-web-dispatch-13/agent-runs/reports/13-component-contribution.md).

---

### Key Additions & Changes

1. **Manifest Declarations**:
   - Updated [`Declarations`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-web-dispatch-13/src/contribution/contract.ts#L46-L54) in [`src/contribution/contract.ts`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-web-dispatch-13/src/contribution/contract.ts) to accept `components?: readonly ComponentDefinition[]`.
   - Imported [`ComponentDefinition`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-web-dispatch-13/src/render/component.ts#L18-L23) cleanly from `../render/component.js`.

2. **Merge & Conflict Resolution**:
   - In [`src/kernel/manifest.ts`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-web-dispatch-13/src/kernel/manifest.ts), added `'component'` to [`Conflict['kind']`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-web-dispatch-13/src/kernel/manifest.ts#L30-L38) and `components: ReadonlyMap<string, Contributed<ComponentDefinition>>` to [`Manifest`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-web-dispatch-13/src/kernel/manifest.ts#L43-L52).
   - In [`mergeManifests()`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-web-dispatch-13/src/kernel/manifest.ts#L106-L198):
     - **Prefix Enforcement**: Enforces that contributed components follow `${id}.${componentName}` (e.g. an extension with `id: 'ui'` must name components `ui.Card`, `ui.Nav`). Any non-conforming name produces a boot-time `manifest.conflicts` entry.
     - **Duplicate Claim Handling**: Employs `claim()` deduplication to log conflicts across contributions at boot time without throwing at render time, preserving the first contributor.

3. **Kernel Startup Wiring**:
   - In [`src/kernel/start.ts`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-web-dispatch-13/src/kernel/start.ts#L234-L238), iterates `kernel.manifest.components.values()` and registers each definition into `components` (`ComponentRegistry`) before mounting chrome or application windows.
   - Closed the reader-audit finding in [`createRegistry().register()`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-web-dispatch-13/src/render/component.ts#L52-L63).

4. **Error Attribution & Diagnostics**:
   - Added `part?: string` to [`RenderOptions`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-web-dispatch-13/src/render/dom.ts#L20-L24).
   - In [`buildElement()`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-web-dispatch-13/src/render/dom.ts#L86-L95), when an unknown component is referenced, errors format as:
     `Unknown component "${node.component}" wanted by "${options.part}". Known: ...`
   - Wired `partOf` from [`src/window/shell.ts`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-web-dispatch-13/src/window/shell.ts#L18-L25) and [`src/window/host.ts`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-web-dispatch-13/src/window/host.ts#L25-L35) back to `kernel.processes.find(p => p.pid === owner)?.applicationId` in [`src/kernel/start.ts`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-web-dispatch-13/src/kernel/start.ts#L252-L260).

